----
> let d = import("data/small.csv")
> d.reg(b ~ a, |
data.reg(formula, [[fe: Terms]], se: classical | robust | hc2 | hc3, cluster: Var, weights: Var, weight_type: frequency | analytic | sampling = sampling, level: Float = 0.95)
    fe: The fixed effects to absorb: a variable, `firm`; several joined by `+`, `firm + year`; an interacted effect joined by `:`, `industry:year`. Int, text, category and date variables all serve; `*`, a range, an expression and the intercept are refused, and so is an effect that is also a variable of the formula.
    (Linear regression by least squares, with fixed effects)
----
> let d = import("data/small.csv")
> d.reg(b ~ a, c, ro|
data.reg(formula, fe: Terms, [[se: classical | robust | hc2 | hc3]], cluster: Var, weights: Var, weight_type: frequency | analytic | sampling = sampling, level: Float = 0.95)
    se: The kind of standard error: `classical`, `robust` (HC1), `hc2` or `hc3`; `classical` unless sampling weights are given, when `robust`. With `fe:`, `hc2` and `hc3` are refused (Z0410), since an observation's leverage in the full design is not available.
    (Linear regression by least squares, with fixed effects)
----
